  "body": "**Blocked by:** #96\n\n## Context\n\nFast mailbox processing requires row actions, bulk operations, flags, and keyboard navigation beyond the view shell.\n\n## Task\n\nAdd row-hover archive, delete, and mark-read/unread actions; bulk selection with the same operations; `j`/`k` movement; and `e` archive. Persist `read` and `flagged` as user-owned generic properties mapped to IMAP `\\\\Seen` and `\\\\Flagged`. Missing legacy booleans display as false. Use the generic relation/property mutation path and preserve selection/focus predictably after mutations.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Hover actions, bulk selection, keyboard controls, focus, read state, and flag state.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Structured search operator parsing, compose/reply, and provider live-sync mechanisms.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Pointer and keyboard users can perform the same triage actions.\n- Bulk operations affect only selected messages and report partial failures.\n- Read/flag changes persist generically and synchronize to the canonical IMAP flags.\n- Keyboard shortcuts do not fire while typing in an editable control.\n",
